      "id": 1,
      "text": "Thorsby was first settled in 1895 and incorporated in 1901 by Scandinavian immigrants seeking a milder climate and fertile soil.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thorsby%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors Thorson, a Swedish settler, with “by” meaning settlement in Scandinavian languages.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thorsby%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A museum inside the old Norwegian Lutheran Church, called Helen Jenkins Chapel, preserves local history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
